# The slc10 copy of slc9-gpu/o2-fullci.env, running BESIDE it rather than
# replacing it: a new CHECK_NAME nobody requires yet, so it can fail freely
# while the packages below are brought up. Retire the slc9 pair, and move the
# name in GitHub branch protection, only once this one is green.
#
# No CONTAINER_IMAGE here, which is the point of the move. slc9 needs
# slc9-gpu-builder because gpu-system.sh resolves ALIBUILD_O2_FORCE_GPU=ci to
# "1" -- detect and require every backend from the image. On slc10 the same
# value resolves to "build", taking CUDA and ROCm from alidist recipes instead,
# so DEFAULTS.env's stock slc10-builder is enough. Same mechanism that already
# removed the need for slc10-gpu-builder; see o2-gpu-test.env beside this file.

CI_NAME=build_O2_fullCI_slc10_x86
CHECK_NAME=build/O2/fullCI-slc10-x86
PACKAGE=O2FullCI
ALIBUILD_DEFAULTS=o2
PR_REPO=AliceO2Group/AliceO2
PR_REPO_CHECKOUT=O2
PR_BRANCH=dev
TRUST_COLLABORATORS=true
DEVEL_PKGS="$PR_REPO $PR_BRANCH $PR_REPO_CHECKOUT
AliceO2Group/O2Physics master
alisw/alidist master
AliceO2Group/O2DPG master"
ALIBUILD_O2_FORCE_GPU=ci
USE_PERF=

# Unlike the slc9 original, which comments on the PR. A check this new will post
# failures that are about slc10 bring-up and not about the pull request, so it
# reports a status and nothing else until it is trustworthy.
DONT_USE_COMMENTS=1

# 12, not the 24 DEFAULTS.env argues for, because this container is ALSO served
# by ci-linux-x86-gpu (CUR_CONTAINER=slc10), which reserves 12 cores and 55296
# MiB on aligpuci -- and REQUIRES_POOL cannot express "any pool but gpu":
# claim-builder.sh matches it exactly against WORKER_NODE_POOL, which
# ci-linux-x86 does not set at all. So a fullCI round can land on the GPU box,
# where 24 compiles inside the ~51 GiB container cap is ~2.1 GiB each. That is
# what OOM-killed ONNXRuntime's flash-attention kernels in o2-gpu-test
# ("nvcc error : cicc died due to signal 9"), and FORCE_GPU=ci builds the same
# CUDA kernels here.
#
# The cost is half the parallelism on the ordinary 24-core workers, which is
# the right trade for a burn-in: an OOM looks like a compile error and would
# make this check's failures unreadable. When it goes production, give fullCI
# its own container directory (added to CUR_CONTAINERS on ci-linux-x86 only)
# and put JOBS back to 24 there -- that excludes the GPU worker structurally
# rather than by detuning everyone.
JOBS=12
